  "content": "Cole's putting has been trending in the wrong direction, and his most recent recorded round is July 10 — 15 days old, so there's nothing on the books for the last two weeks specifically.\n\n**Over his last 15 recorded rounds (May 18 – Jul 10):**\n- Strokes gained putting: **-3.91** per round (higher is better; negative means he's losing strokes to the field on the greens)\n- Putts per round: **32.9**\n- Three-putt rate: **10.3%** of holes\n- One-putt rate: **26.8%** of holes\n\n**Trend (last 10 rounds, May 29 – Jul 10):** average SG putting of -4.68, and it's worsening — his last three rounds were -4.71, -5.34, and -7.61, the two weakest readings in the whole window.\n\n**Where it's breaking down (same window, by distance):**\n| Distance | Make rate | Attempts |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3-5 ft | 46.5% | 43 |\n| 5-10 ft | 27.7% | 83 |\n| 10-15 ft | 15.6% | 64 |\n| 15-25 ft | 12.2% | 49 |\n| 25+ ft | 0% | 31 |\n\nThe 0-3 ft bucket shows a value but has 0 recorded attempts, so treat that one as not measured. The clearest pattern is a steep drop-off starting at 5-10 ft and getting worse from there — that, combined with the last-three-round slide, is where I'd focus a putting session before his next event.\n\n_Some figures in this answer could not be traced back to your program's data, so I've flagged it rather than presenting them as fact. Please ask again._",
